Pros:
-Black, white and red look nice together
Cons:
-Jankiest animations i've seen in a long time;
-Terrible pacing;
-The most bored Voice Actors of all time;
-Endless camera pans;
-Absolutely linear "experience";
-No plot "hook" to get you interested in how it ends;
-Bizzare sound mixing, there might be about 3 different background tracks playing at the same time;
-Jarring leaps in asset quality;
-Detective board that literally spells out for you what to do and which you can't fail.
Straight line walking sim with no actual depth, with an episode that can be completed under two hours.

Very promising early access survival game.
When I first heard about this game the thing that kept my interest and made me take a look at it was, that this is a survivor game without zombies and this kind of nonsense. You're playing for a man survived a plane crash in Canadian Taiga. So in this game your main enemys are cold and predators like wolves.
Before buying the game I've been playing a pirate version for a pretty long period to see if it worth buying and to see how do devs respond to players feedback.
I'm not good at writing reviews, so I'll just write a features list. But first let me remind you: The game is in alpha! It is already worth buying and I think it can only become better.
­­­— Very promising game setting;
— There will be a story when it'll be finished; (for now it's just a sandbox)
— Great atmosphere;
— Nice cartoonish graphic;
— Goog gameplay;
I wont list negative aspects, because I'm sure they'll be gone by the time the game will come out.

